      "@id": "https://api.nuget.org/v3/catalog0/data/2026.09.27.17.56.29/invarix.gate.evidence.1.0.0-rc.1.json#deprecation/alternatePackage",
      "id": "Invarix.Gate.Evidence",
      "range": "[1.0.0-rc.3, )"
    },
    "message": "Superseded by 1.0.0-rc.3 of the Invarix.Gate packages. rc.3 fixes approval requests that could carry credentials unmasked (advisory INVARIX-2026-001, https://invarix.dk/security), an Agent Framework defect that, in enforce mode and with no GateRunScope, terminated every run once the agent's total tool calls passed the per-run ceiling, and the evidence recorded for approvals nobody answered. The rc.2 README's example policy ran 3 of the 11 detectors; re-check any policy copied from it.",
    "reasons": [
      "Other",
      "CriticalBugs"
    ]
  },
  "description": "Writes Invarix.Gate tool-call verdicts into an Invarix.Guard.Evidence decision log. Every verdict the action firewall renders becomes a CloudEvents 1.0 decision record: the tool that was asked for, the SHA-256 digest of the exact canonical arguments, each rule that matched as a detector result, the outcome, and the operator who approved or refused an escalation. Mapping runs on the tool-call thread and the write is handed to a bounded background queue, so an agent never waits on evidence I/O and a broken evidence store never breaks a run. Requires a commercial Gate license.",
  "iconFile": "nuget-icon-128.png",
  "id": "Invarix.Gate.Evidence",
